    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d456">

                <pb facs="0608" n="464" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg464"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 Holleman, C.H./9: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-06-05T16:00:00+08:00">June 5, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>447. My 439, June 1, 7 p.m.</p>
                <p>1. Following from American Consul at Amoy: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“June 4, 3 p.m. Letter received from Holleman byLungyenchou Chinese
                            stating that he escaped 28th and was making his way toward Taipu where
                            he is trying to reach Swatow. Believed that owing to conditions in
                            Swatow district his arrival there may be delayed or he may have to
                            return overland to Amoy via Pingwo. Chinese authorities <pb facs="0609"
                                n="465" xml:id="pg465"/> trying to inform General Chang Chen
                            requesting verification and protection. Have telegraphed Berger<anchor
                                n="74" xml:id="d456-f1"/> requesting him try to verify and render
                            any assistance possible.”<anchor n="75" xml:id="d456-f2"/></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d456-f1" n="74" xml:id="d456-f1-content">
                <p>David C. Berger, Consul at Swatow.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d456-f2" n="75" xml:id="d456-f2-content">
                <p>The Minister in China in telegram No. 501, June 24, reported Dr. Holleman’s safe
                    arrival at Amoy from Swatow (393.1111 Holleman, C.H./29).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
